<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Project 2 Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00662</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Project 2 Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>af6222b1-e98f-4786-bb6b-06d83824d885</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">In this culminating project, you will integrate the ideas from the unit and engage in
        multiple aspects of mathematical modeling.</para>

      <para id="para-00002">In the first activity, you interpret and analyze given models that represent the
        constraints and conditions in a situation. In the second activity, you create your own
        models after specifying quantities of interest, identifying relevant information, and
        setting the constraints.</para>
      </section>
      <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Project Activities</title>
      <list list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
        <item>Determining a Solution to Inequalities</item>
        <item>Interpret a Set of Mathematical Models</item>
        <item>Perform Mathematical Modeling</item>
      </list>
    </section>

<section id="sect-00003">
      <title>Learning Targets</title>
      <para id="para-00003">When you finish this project, you will have demonstrated how to:</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>Interpret inequalities and graphs in a mathematical model. </item>
        <item>Choose variables, specify the constraints, and write inequalities to create a
          mathematical model. </item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
